  "contract": [
    "flags=0 resolves only a currently installed committed record. A merely parsed/loaded APK is not package existence. Requested record publication/identity is validated by existing registry code.",
    "A bounded file-backed ZIP reader reads the central directory and AndroidManifest.xml only; it does not extract DEX/resources/native libraries or scan other APK payloads. APK length and manifest package/version fields must agree with the requested record.",
    "PackageInfo snapshots contain actual packageName, low API26 int versionCode, nullable literal versionName, and fresh ApplicationInfo. Missing versionCode defaults to 0; missing versionName is null.",
    "ApplicationInfo exposes proven package/class names, data directory, SDK values, label/icon/theme IDs and nonlocalized label. Unproven flags/UID/nativeLibraryDir/process metadata remain unavailable.",
    "Own sourceDir/publicSourceDir is emitted only when captured running installation revision/hash/size matches the requested record. A newer installed revision cannot reuse the running old alias. Cross-package source APK mounts are unavailable.",
    "Unknown, uninstalled, malformed and case-mismatched names throw real NameNotFoundException. Null with flags=0 throws that exception with an actual null Java message. The exception is materialized before transport diagnostic frames can change the Java-observable message.",
    "Registration of the checked NameNotFoundException hierarchy uses AndroidException -> Exception -> Throwable -> Object. SDK catches validate that ancestry.",
    "Returned metadata is a mutable snapshot; mutating it does not change registry values. GC follows real field edges to ApplicationInfo and strings, then reclaims discarded snapshots without a permanent service cache.",
    "Nonzero flags, unproven fields, and resource-valued versionName fail explicitly rather than returning invented times/signatures/flags/versions. A resource-valued application boolean does not reject unrelated proven PackageInfo fields.",
    "Shared SDK parser default targetSdk now uses the effective child minSdk. Normal SDK fixtures prove min-only26->target26 and empty/absent uses-sdk -> min1,target1."
  ],
